id: pm-jev-vouf
title: Detect existing duplicate items with calibrated pair decisions
description: "Add bounded title and body lexical candidates, sequential typed pair verification, abstention and explicit SDK apply/close receipts. Measure lexical and local model arms on public duplicate closures with held-out labels."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-19T15:15:26.929Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-19T23:01:40.562Z"
author: codex-agent
parent: pm-jev-0w3q
comments[26]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-19T15:15:41.354Z",codex-agent,"Plan: preserve pre-create title screening; add bounded pair scanning over certified complete SDK reads, sequential noul verification, a symmetric abstain band, and explicit apply/close authorization with receipts. Evaluate public tracker-copy duplicate closures versus lexical hard controls, using disjoint duplicate groups and a maximum of 200 pairs per local model arm. Canonical checkouts and external data remain read-only."
  "2026-10-19T15:23:37.144Z",codex-agent,"Implemented real-SDK pair scans and mutation guards. Focused pair regressions pass, including abstention, confidence authorization, explicit close gating, receipt history, read-only scans and model-unavailable refusal. Public evaluation inventory: 29 verified public copies; 2 skipped before tracker reads. Strict resolvable labels yield 35 positives (31 historical consolidation receipts plus 4 standard closures), paired with 70 lexical controls. Duplicate-group hashing separates dev and held-out items; retrieval misses count as false negatives. Calls run sequentially under nice."
  "2026-10-19T15:27:55.026Z",codex-agent,"Independent behavioral revert proofs: disabling only the positive probability cutoff makes the real-tracker apply regression fail (duplicate versus abstain); forcing closure without checking the extra close flag makes it fail (closed versus open). Source restored byte-for-byte; the same focused test passes 1/1. Command: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"pair apply writes only above threshold\" test/dedupe.test.ts. Threshold selection is dev-F1 with a 0.8 model floor; this is an operating-point calibration, not a 95% precision guarantee. Lexical controls are closed-world labels and may contain unrecorded duplicates."
  "2026-10-19T15:37:27.170Z",codex-agent,"Real-label held-out evaluation: 24 pairs (8 positives,16 lexical controls), dev 81 (27/54); 35 real positive closures overall, 8 retrieval misses overall and 1 held out. Lexical: precision 30.4%, recall 87.5%, F1 45.2%, abstain 0%, 62.0 ms/pair. tev1:0.8b: precision 46.2%, recall 75.0%, F1 57.1%, abstain 41.7%, 892.5 ms/pair. tev1:4b: precision/recall/F1 62.5%, abstain 16.7%, 5571.7 ms/pair. Wilson intervals and F1 envelope are in README and calibration/dedupe-report-v1.json. Total elapsed 810.5 s; 107 sequential calls/model including an excluded identical-text control and a counted replacement repetition after postprocessing failure. Cutoffs use dev-F1, 0.8 model floor, three positive predictions and one true positive. Controls remain closed-world labels; small correlated samples and weak precision preclude a readiness claim."
  "2026-10-19T15:42:22.242Z",codex-agent,"Packed CLI dogfood: pm --json jev dedupe --status open returned 20 rows on the copied public pm-github tracker using real tev1:4b. Authoritative tracker byte hashes were identical before and after. The final candidate implementation reproduces every packed-run pair after the exact-text fallback correction; all 105 benchmark pairs/scores also remain identical. The PR will include the first ten complete verdict rows. SDK/UX observations: the pinned SDK provides related but no duplicate-of mutation kind, and update plus closure emits separate history events. Normal-home health sees an existing global pm-github host-version skew; isolated CI identity is used for package gates."
  "2026-10-19T15:44:35.427Z",codex-agent,"Final linked runner passed 3/3 commands: the focused real-tracker and artifact replay suite, npm release:check and bun release:check. Both release gates used disposable HOME with global/system Git configuration disabled and unchanged coverage/duplication thresholds. All coverage dimensions are 100%; duplication is zero. Strict health passes with merge drivers under isolated HOME; normal HOME still reports the unrelated global extension host-version skew. No items were closed; claim will be released for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-19T15:46:19.699Z",codex-agent,Fresh git clone --no-local verification of implementation commit e360669 passes strict health with required merge drivers and all four commit-identity tests. The clone uses the pinned installed dependencies and isolated HOME/Git identity; authoritative tracked files remain unchanged. Implementation source and measured artifacts are identical to the npm/Bun gate inputs. Claim is released and the item remains in_progress for orchestrator review.
  "2026-10-19T15:47:13.762Z",codex-agent,"Opened PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-jev/pull/30 with the full real-label evaluation, independent revert proofs, npm/Bun gate counts and the first ten read-only pm-github verdict rows. No merge or release is part of this task. The remaining delivery receipt changes documentation and this append-only tracker evidence only."
  "2026-10-19T16:48:30.161Z",codex-agent,"PR 30 round 1: reviewed the latest review body; one pair-alignment finding and no outside-diff findings. Plan: persist repository:a:b identity in samples and model observations, assert exact sample order before split assignment, and reject a metric-preserving cross-split swap. Preserve existing inference scores and provenance; no model calls. Reuse this feature item for review evidence."
  "2026-10-19T16:50:52.731Z",codex-agent,"Round 1 implemented: labelledPairs now emits stable repository:a:b ids; original evaluation/progress and finalization drivers persist them. Backfilled all 105 sample rows and each retained model observation from trusted script order, plus excluded-observation identity from the original sample receipt. No inference rerun. Structural comparison after removing only added identity fields proves every existing report value unchanged. Replay asserts length, exact ids, labels and retrieval metadata before splitting. Metric-preserving cross-split swaps (0.8b indices 2/81; 4b indices 0/83) retain thresholds and all dev/held-out metrics but are rejected. Independent revert proofs: reverting only labelledPairs causes the benchmark identity regression to fail; removing only identity checks causes the swap regression to fail with Missing expected exception. Restored focused suite passes 5/5."
  "2026-10-19T16:52:38.999Z",codex-agent,Initial npm/Bun gates identified four duplicated test lines in metric replay at the unchanged zero-duplication threshold. Extracted a shared metric assertion so normal replay and swap regression exercise identical metric checks. No threshold changes. Rerunning both complete gates and focused tests.
  "2026-10-19T17:03:36.990Z",codex-agent,"Round 1 final verification: pm-linked runner passes 4/4 commands (timeout 1800 seconds). Focused tracker/replay suite passes 15/15; isolated-identity npm run release:check and bun run release:check each pass 218/218 tests; focused receipt suite passes 5/5. Both release gates retain 100% statements, branches, functions and lines (4955/4955 statements and lines; 1921/1921 branches; 191/191 functions), zero duplication across 51 sources, and no production audit findings. Source and all pre-existing measurements remain unchanged after the passing gates. Accepted limitation: historical observation alignment is trusted from the producing script order, explicitly documented in README and the PR; inference was not rerun. No additional outside-diff findings or new PM CLI/SDK defects were found. Releasing the claim and leaving this item in_progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-19T18:52:47.670Z",codex-agent,"Review round 2 verified all three unresolved PR 30 findings at 345c235. Latest review has no outside-diff findings. Plan: normalize fallback identities; validate receipt deadline and post-link source revision under the separate close lock; share the run signal with both digest reads. Add real-tracker concurrent-edit and expiry regressions plus individual behavioral revert proofs."
  "2026-10-19T18:57:38.850Z",codex-agent,"Implemented normalized semantic fallback identities, shared deadline signals for both digest reads with typed timeout translation, and a live post-link authorization fingerprint captured under the item lock and consumed by the separate close guard. Focused suite passes 19/19, including independent real SDK clients editing body/comments between link and close, exact deadline expiry, historical receipt refusal, unchanged successful close, and first/final delayed digest reads. The close refusal preserves the prior relation and receipt."
  "2026-10-19T19:00:14.382Z",codex-agent,"Independent behavioral revert proofs ran in disposable source copies with the new regressions unchanged: reverting only candidatePairs fails the normalized-stopgram test (1/1); reverting only guardDedupeMutation fails body edit, comment edit, receipt removal, deadline expiry and historical receipt refusal (5/6; unchanged closure still passes); reverting only verifyModel fails the delayed digest regressions. Tests import TypeScript directly, so no stale dist can mask the proofs. The initial linked runner used its default 120-second timeout; final gates will use 1800 seconds."
  "2026-10-19T19:05:35.764Z",codex-agent,"Final guard also binds the live snapshot to the matching directed receipt and close reason: a different canonical is refused, receipt removal cannot bypass the live snapshot, and historical duplicate receipts do not block later ordinary completion. Tests cover unchanged closure, concurrent body/comment changes, receipt removal, deadline expiry, historical reuse and a different canonical. Source is now frozen for final npm/Bun release gates; prior preliminary gates are superseded by the final run."
  "2026-10-19T19:14:11.579Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 final frozen-source verification passed. Independent behavioral reverts: candidatePairs fails 1/1 normalized retrieval regression; guardDedupeMutation fails 6/7 close cases while unchanged closure passes; verifyModel fails both delayed digest regressions. Restored focused tracker suite passes 22/22 and artifact receipt suite 5/5. Final PM-linked release selection passes 2/2 commands: isolated-identity npm run release:check and bun run release:check each pass 230/230 tests. Coverage is 100% statements/lines (4985/4985), branches (1952/1952) and functions (193/193); zero duplication across 51 sources and zero production audit findings. Frozen source hashes remain unchanged. The preliminary mixed-source coverage result is superseded. No new PM CLI/SDK defect was found; the runner default timeout required an explicit 1800-second limit. Existing limitation: the canonical target has no joint cross-item lock. Releasing the claim for orchestrator verification; leave this item in_progress."
  "2026-10-19T20:40:53.867Z",codex-agent,"Review round 3: fetched all review threads and every unresolved comment; exactly two unresolved findings (PRRT_kwDOU8IMzs6uFcIg, PRRT_kwDOU8IMzs6uFcIo). Latest CodeRabbit review has no outside-diff findings and all current required CI checks pass. Both findings are valid: pair scans reject a valid shared confidence default below 0.5, and delivery counts are stale. Plan: distinguish explicit flags from configured defaults, retain the calibrated safety floor, test real-tracker preview/apply behavior and explicit invalid flags, then refresh documented counts with executable documentation checks. Merged origin/main before changes; no pending merge receipts. Normal-home health has unrelated global extension host-version skew; isolated-identity health passes with two existing stale-item advisories."
  "2026-10-19T20:42:15.372Z",codex-agent,"Implemented explicit-only pair confidence validation and clamping of valid shared defaults. Real-SDK regression covers defaults 0 and 0.3, unchanged tracker bytes below the 0.8 safety floor, inclusive application at 0.8 with a receipt, invalid explicit flags, a higher 0.95 configured default, the underscore flag alias, and the measured model cutoff. Documentation now separates the focused tracker suite, artifact receipt suite and two release commands; counts will be confirmed by final gates. The executable documentation regression is linked on this item rather than adding a runtime source test for prose."
  "2026-10-19T20:42:45.064Z",codex-agent,"Independent round 3 revert proofs: restoring only the prior runPairDedupe confidence handling leaves the new real-tracker test unchanged and fails 1/1 with the erroneous pair-confidence rejection for an omitted flag. Restoring the prior README leaves the linked documentation regression unchanged and fails with stale 217/217 delivery text. Both files restored byte-for-byte; the focused confidence test and linked documentation check pass. Full source verification follows with unchanged thresholds. PM file linking requires repeated --add flags for separate bare paths; the comma-bearing shorthand was rejected and corrected without changing tracker data."
  "2026-10-19T20:54:06.079Z",codex-agent,"Round 3 final unchanged-source gates pass through the PM-linked runner: 2/2 selected release commands, each under disposable HOME with global/system Git identity disabled and an 1800-second timeout. npm run release:check and bun run release:check each pass 231/231 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todos. Focused tracker tests pass 23/23; the separate artifact receipt suite passes 5/5 (combined 28/28). Linked documentation assertion passes 1/1. Both independent reverts fail as recorded above. Coverage remains 100% in all four dimensions across 18 runtime/script TypeScript sources: 4986/4986 statements and lines, 1954/1954 branches, 193/193 functions. Duplication is zero across 51 sources, production audit is clean, changelog and publication-attestation checks pass. Calibration measurements and dependency pins are unchanged. No new PM CLI/SDK defect was found. Existing limitations remain: no joint source/target lock and partial evaluation receipts tracked separately in pm-jev-w1zj."
  "2026-10-19T20:54:49.918Z",codex-agent,"Fresh git clone --no-local of implementation commit 28ab04d passes pm health --strict-exit --json with the pinned dependencies, required merge drivers and isolated HOME/Git identity. All four commit identity/privacy tests pass; tracked clone files remain unchanged. Health retains only the two existing stale in-progress advisories. Releasing the claim for orchestrator verification; this item remains in_progress. No review thread replies, resolutions, bot mentions, merge or release were performed."
  "2026-10-19T21:47:21.433Z",pi-agent,"PR 30 review round: two review threads remain open (README delivery-check counts, dedupe --title help text). Verifying both against the current code and gate output."
  "2026-10-19T22:04:03.028Z",pi-agent,"PR 30 review round: fixed the dedupe --title help finding (index.ts). The flag description no longer claims --title is required; it now says 'Pre-create screening: title of the item about to be created; omit to scan existing pairs', and the dedupe help examples gained a pair-scan example ('pm jev dedupe --limit-pairs 20') while keeping both title-screening examples. Revert proof: restoring the old '(required)' description and dropping the pair-scan example makes the new registration-contract test fail with 'The input did not match the regular expression /Pre-create screening/'; the fixed tree passes it."
  "2026-10-19T22:04:13.387Z",pi-agent,"PR 30 review round: README delivery-check counts re-verified against the current gate output. Full suite now runs 232/232 tests (231 before this round plus the new help-contract regression), focused tracker/replay suite still 23/23, separate artifact receipt suite 5/5, pm-linked release selection 2/2. README updated from 231/231 to 232/232; the other counts were already exact. Regression: the documentation assertion command now asserts 232/232 in README and fails if the text drifts."
  "2026-10-19T22:58:28.489Z",pi-agent,"PR 30 review round gates: full release gate passes on both runners at unchanged thresholds. npm run release:check exit 0 and bun run release:check exit 0, each with disposable HOME and global/system Git configuration disabled: 232/232 tests, coverage 100% lines/branches/functions, duplication zero, pm-linked release selection unchanged, changelog check clean, release attestation verified. pm health strict exit fails only on a pre-existing global pm-github extension host version skew in this environment; history_drift is clean and no merge receipts are pending (no merge was needed this round: the branch head already contains origin/main)."
